body:
Demo project is online,
https://github.com/silnarm/pathing-demo

Note/Warning: It includes an extension and godot_cpp as a submodule, and currently has no build instructions ;-P
Note2/Warning2: I can not guarantee the extension will compile on Windows (but it should).

`master` branch is the 'base' demo, without the 'fixed' navmesh pathing; will run on 4.6.
`testing` branch is the one for a modified engine, adding pathing with the proposed fix, test-runs and statistics collection & reporting.

In the `testing` branch `NavigationServer2D` is expected to sport a (script exposed) `map_get_path2` method to return the path calculated with the fix.

Changes I made to support this:

Add enumeration value `PathfindingAlgorithm::PATHFINDING_ALGORITHM_ASTAR_2`
duplicate `GodotNavigationServer2D::map_get_path()` to `GodotNavigationServer2D::map_get_path2()`
fix things up (declare it in `NavigationServer2D`, no-op implement in `NavigationServer2DDummy`)
change `map_get_path2()` to use `PATHFINDING_ALGORITHM_ASTAR_2` in the query task
in `NavMeshQueries2D::map_query_path()` add the new enum to the switch() ~line:185
in `NavMeshQueries2D::_query_task_search_polygon_connections()`:
  replace the `if (new_traveled_distance < neighbor_poly.traveled_distance) {...}` (including if body) with:
```
	float new_distance_to_destination = new_entry.distance_to(p_end_point) * connection_owner->get_travel_cost();
	bool update = false;
	if (p_query_task.pathfinding_algorithm == PathfindingAlgorithm::PATHFINDING_ALGORITHM_ASTAR) {
		update = new_traveled_distance < neighbor_poly.traveled_distance;
	} else {
		float new_total_travel_cost = new_traveled_distance + new_distance_to_destination;
		update = new_total_travel_cost < neighbor_poly.total_travel_cost() && !Math::is_equal_approx(new_total_travel_cost, neighbor_poly.total_travel_cost());
	}

	if (update) {
		// Add the polygon to the heap of polygons to traverse next.
		neighbor_poly.back_navigation_poly_id = p_least_cost_id;
		neighbor_poly.back_navigation_edge = p_connection.edge;
		neighbor_poly.back_navigation_edge_pathway_start = p_connection.pathway_start;
		neighbor_poly.back_navigation_edge_pathway_end = p_connection.pathway_end;
		neighbor_poly.traveled_distance = new_traveled_distance;
		neighbor_poly.distance_to_destination = new_distance_to_destination;
		neighbor_poly.entry = new_entry;

		if (neighbor_poly.traversable_poly_index != traversable_polys.INVALID_INDEX) {
			traversable_polys.shift(neighbor_poly.traversable_poly_index);
		} else {
			neighbor_poly.poly = p_connection.polygon;
			traversable_polys.push(&neighbor_poly);
		}
	}
```
Optional, but recommended to reduce precision issues when comparing path lengths:
in `NavMeshQueries2D::_query_task_post_process_corridorfunnel()` comment out the calls to `_query_task_clip_path()`

I was unable to figure out why those extra points (path/mesh-edge intersection points) are being calculated and added to the path, seems like something that we should only be doing in some kind debug post-processor, can't imagine people are happy about paying for something they probably don't want. That is an issue for another day though.
